                        ],
                        "form": "more conversant"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "4d1fa17e-0a7b-479d-8778-8049f87b4c57",
                        "entry_id": "2caa6e11-ceb4-36c1-8984-64edb9c59358",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most conversant"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7621f85b-01af-3fa9-850d-62619f59fa28",
                        "entry_id": "2caa6e11-ceb4-36c1-8984-64edb9c59358",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Closely familiar; current; having frequent interaction."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "032b9c87-b900-4ab0-88ac-52f927f0680c",
                                "sense_id": "7621f85b-01af-3fa9-850d-62619f59fa28",
                                "text": "VVe (of all earthlings) are Gods vtmoſt ſubiects, the laſt (in a manner) that he bought to his obedience: ſhal we then forgette that vvee are any ſubiects of hys, becauſe (as amongſt his Angels) he is not viſibly conuerſant amongſt vs?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "195927cd-a3ab-3fd5-b8ff-2e733bf41aa1",
                        "entry_id": "2caa6e11-ceb4-36c1-8984-64edb9c59358",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Familiar or acquainted by use or study; well-informed; versed."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "88290f42-3b87-4a3b-88b3-efc695b38727",
                                "sense_id": "195927cd-a3ab-3fd5-b8ff-2e733bf41aa1",
                                "text": "She is equally conversant with Shakespeare and the laws of physics."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5aefcaeb-de1a-402f-9b5a-41b19014906a",
                                "sense_id": "195927cd-a3ab-3fd5-b8ff-2e733bf41aa1",
                                "text": "We ſee in all things how deſuetude do's contract and narrow our faculties, ſo that we may apprehend only thoſe things wherein we are converſant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "13e7f6d9-3efe-4ed4-98c4-c85b73cf6d42",
                                "sense_id": "195927cd-a3ab-3fd5-b8ff-2e733bf41aa1",
                                "text": "c. 1694, John Dryden, letter to Mr. John Dennis\ndeeply conversant in the Platonic philosophy"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ccbfb96-80be-4495-b646-85e59e2676a5",
                                "sense_id": "195927cd-a3ab-3fd5-b8ff-2e733bf41aa1",
                                "text": "1720, Thomas Parnell, corrected by Alexander Pope, \"Essay on Homer\", published with Pope's translation of the Iliad\nHe uses the different dialects […] as one who had been conversant with them all."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "74d79440-9713-3b60-9231-9db599268c3c",
                        "entry_id": "2caa6e11-ceb4-36c1-8984-64edb9c59358",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Concerned; occupied."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9b4ab45c-89d8-4c63-86dd-bdb615679997",
                                "sense_id": "74d79440-9713-3b60-9231-9db599268c3c",
                                "text": "If any think education, because it is conversant about children, to be but a private and domestick duty, he has been ignorantly bred himself."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3e09fa65-96cc-4646-abad-fa0141a9d456",
                                "sense_id": "74d79440-9713-3b60-9231-9db599268c3c",
                                "text": "Their Ideas are perpetually converſant in Lines and Figures. If they would, for example, praiſe the Beauty of a Woman, or any other Animal, they deſcribe it by Rhombs, Circles, Parallelograms, Ellipſes, and other Geometrical Terms, or by Words of Art drawn from Muſick, needleſs here to repeat."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8de1f25b-d5e8-4051-8554-e1a52a9f168b",
